The important part is what happens internally:

TURN 1

Model
   ↓
eval
   ↓
const courseFees = [400, 700, 600]
   ↓
QuickJS Interpreter
   ↓
Variable remains in REPL


Then:

TURN 2

Same thread_id
   ↓
eval
   ↓
courseFees already exists
   ↓
Average + maximum calculated


So unlike:
execute("python script.py")

which launches a shell/process, the Interpreter gives the agent a persistent QuickJS REPL. It has no normal filesystem,
network, process, or require access unless capabilities are explicitly exposed.
